045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504560 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504560 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186504274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504560 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b021d4b8-9d31-550f-8894-f27be8d6ecdd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504578 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186504191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504578 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186504272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504578 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186504330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504578 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186504370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504578 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186504435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504578 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504578 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504578 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186504370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504578 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cdc675dd-7a38-5eec-ad05-1b9e422a82c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504608 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504608 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125530" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504608 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504608 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the $72.9$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}\\sqrt{x},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504608 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "158dc85d-a65b-564b-ba7e-be30418efec3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504608 #edb/ref 1074 "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${x}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {x}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $72.9$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.729.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {x}_{0.729}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{{x}_{0.729}}\\frac{3}{16}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{8}|}_{0}^{{x}_{0.729}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{0.729}^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $72.9$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}_{0.729}^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{8} & =0.729 \\\\ {x}_{0.729}^{\\frac{1}{2}} & =\\sqrt[3]{(8)(0.729)} \\\\ {x}_{0.729}^{\\frac{1}{2}} & =(2)(0.9) \\\\ {x}_{0.729} & =(1.8)^{2} \\\\ {x}_{0.729} & =3.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504616 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504616 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94622" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504616 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504616 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the median of the random variable $Y$ if the probability density function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y},\\, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504616 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "328730e5-b32c-5f55-aef8-1fdf6d6f55ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504616 #edb/ref 1074 "The median of a random variable $Y$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le m) & ={\\int }_{0}^{m}{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{e}^{-y}{|}_{0}^{m} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {e}^{-m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -m & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ -m & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ m & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504646 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504646 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504646 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504646 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the $60$th percentile of the random variable $Y$ if the probability distribution function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}},\\, & y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504646 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7f1b2358-54f2-52cf-a9df-c46a72812503" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504646 #edb/ref 1074 "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $Y$ is the number ${y}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le {y}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $60$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.6.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le {y}_{0.6}) & ={\\int }_{1}^{{y}_{0.6}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{y}|}_{1}^{{y}_{0.6}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{y}_{0.6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $60$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{{y}_{0.6}} & =0.6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}_{0.6}} & =0.4 \\\\ {y}_{0.6} & =\\frac{1}{0.4} \\\\ {y}_{0.6} & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504676 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504676 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125715" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504676 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504676 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504676 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c3057bfc-a8d8-5a19-9075-be23799b04aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504676 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{q}_{1}^{6}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{q}_{1}^{6}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{q}_{1}} & =\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{4}{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{q}_{3}^{6}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{q}_{3}^{6}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{q}_{1}} & =\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\sqrt[6]{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}IQR & ={q}_{3}-{q}_{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[6]{4}-\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{4}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504702 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504702 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94668" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504702 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504702 #edb/ref 1071 "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504702 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2b4a0b2-77c3-5ed8-8555-0cfe3f01b758" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504702 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{q}_{1}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {q}_{1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{q}_{3}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {q}_{3} & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\nIQR={q}_{3}-{q}_{1}=2\\sqrt{3}-2≈1.464\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504710 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186504726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504710 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "01cc5e7e-84c9-528b-a9ef-d7f70750a185" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504710 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186504616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504715 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1e906454-9530-5253-a6c1-cda94270f061" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504715 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186504676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504720 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186504721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504720 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "44882186-3aa7-55b0-9985-fbfa449cb9fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504720 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186504646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504721 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186504715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504721 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "44dd1ada-9d95-5d13-8839-831e39188195" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504721 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186504608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504726 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186504720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504726 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "62be2f38-fa1c-5afd-b03f-11afbcfda04d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504726 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186504702 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
